# Network threading

Blocking network I/O must not run on the GUI / main thread. On Android this
throws `NetworkOnMainThreadException` and the request never leaves the device.

## C++

Use `GetPlatform().RunTask(Platform::Thread::Network, ...)` for
`platform::HttpClient` and any other blocking fetch. Hop results that mutate
UI-owned state back with `Platform::Thread::Gui`. Follow `FriendsManager`.

Do not call `HttpClient`, `IdentityStore` HTTP (claim / leave / delete /
report), `FetchAreaSnapshot`, or similar from a GUI-thread JNI entry unless
that entry is documented `@WorkerThread` and the Java caller has already hopped.

## Android Java

- Call HTTP JNI from `ThreadPool.getWorker()`, then `UiThread.run()` for UI.
  Follow `MyAccountDialogFragment`, `OsmLoginFragment`, and
  `StreetPixelsManager.requestCompetitionAreaSnapshot`.
- Mark blocking HTTP natives `@WorkerThread`.
- Bind cached / local state on the UI thread first; refresh when the worker
  returns. Do not `get()` or wait on the UI thread.
- Map downloads already use `ChunkTask` / WorkManager; do not add a new
  GUI-thread download path.
